# Virtual Search found_by repair

Issue 121, source parent 77880f9b489b2e97653345c27d10caeadd900031.
Its execute.ts remains the engine ec720020f module before this correction.
No transaction, upload cleanup, event snapshot or history-summary change is
included in this repair.

## Reproduction and contract

The unchanged independent attacker fixture comes from
60049d11732a31bea561dd9b2c4a2cc8fd8de95f. Both copies have SHA-256
5fda46541add668ca4893fab64ca3c29ad2acc56894dff628c694c9d9bd7210e.
It opens the committed synthetic SQLite deck read-only. Direct Image type
queries return existing cards, while all three found_by queries targeting
Image+*type with by-name/create/update rights fail as invalid Basic cards.
The original found_by method fetches fabricated cards and consumes their
cql_hash. The existing fetch pipeline already defines the VirtualSearch
family's code-defined recipes and codename-based membership.

The missing branch was in found_by's fabricated-card resolver: only pattern
sets were considered. It now consults the existing VirtualSearch codename
registry rather than inventing a second recipe table or matching display
name suffixes. Nested found_by runs in the virtual card's name context, so
its _left target resolves through the existing set query. The codename is
read once and reused for the existing pattern fallback.

## Verification

All three unchanged attacker cases pass after correction. An exact-parent
source-load override reproduces the three failures again without reverting
the production working file. Baseline source, override, raw failure output
and before/after JUnit remain locally under .runtime/foundby121.

Five focused suites report 72 passed, zero failed/skipped: the attacker
fixture, new virtual-search controls, existing found-by hash and ID-projection
suites, and the execution suite. Additional real SQLite controls cover a
renamed anchor resolved by codename, root-owned paging, actor read filtering,
trash exclusion and invalid unknown-right/Basic targets. Whole-tree TypeScript
checking and diff whitespace checks pass.

Tests execute real local SQLite and source; transformation caches may be
reused, not verdicts. No model, hosted service, original site, new dependency
or deployment was used. Independent re-attack on the controller's integrated
candidate and full-port acceptance remain separate requirements.

An additional invalid-codename control exposed a preexisting lookup defect:
codename constructor inherited Object.constructor from the set-override object,
spread that function into an empty statement, and returned every live fixture
card instead of rejecting the target. The set-override fallback now requires an
own property. The new control fails before that guard and passes after it;
this is a local query-shaping failure, not a claim of a deployed data exposure.
The final five-suite run with this control reports 73 passed, zero failed or
skipped; whole-tree TypeScript checking and whitespace checks pass.
